      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin:0;">Anfield is known for its tightly packed Victorian terraces. They were built from the 1870s to the 1900s for workers at the north Liverpool docks. Many still have their original cast iron waste pipes, now well over 100 years old. The terraces are built so close together that a burst pipe or leak can quickly spread to the house next door.

Anfield has a lot of private rented homes. Liverpool City Council runs a selective licensing scheme here. Landlords must keep their homes to a set standard, including working heating and hot water. We do <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-liverpool" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">gas safety certificates</a> for Anfield landlords. We go straight to tenants in an emergency. We give you the paperwork the council asks for. <a href="/boiler-service-liverpool" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">Annual boiler services</a> cost £120 across the whole of L4.</p>
